body: "Gemini review on unbraind/pm-cli#62 flagged that pm-changelog@2026.5.24-13 full-history generation lists matching git release tags and then shells out once per tag to resolve commit timestamps.\\n\\nExpected: full-history generation should use one formatted git tag/ref query for matching tags and parse timestamps in-process, so runtime scales with tracker data rather than process startup count.\\n\\nTracked in pm as pmc-99tc.\n\n---\n\n### GitHub comments (1)\n\n> **@unbraind** (2026-05-24T16:10:18Z)\n>\n> Fixed in pm-changelog@2026.5.24-14. The implementation now resolves release tag names and peeled/direct commit timestamps with one formatted git tag lookup, includes annotated-tag commit-date regression coverage, and passed the Daily Release workflow run 26366186354."
